if (ret) {
    kobject_put(&type->kobj);
}
```
Reason:
The fix replaces `kfree(type)` with `kobject_put(&type->kobj)`, which properly decrements the reference count of the `kobject`. This ensures that the memory associated with the `kobject` is cleaned up correctly, preventing the memory leak when `kobject_init_and_add()` fails.

